    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #293\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed successfully to branch `bb/relay-108-module-contract-01-12-implement-manife-thr_x2584gcrs8` (existing PR #293).\n\n## Summary\n\nAddressed the code-review findings from PR #293:\n\n- **Unmet acceptance criterion**: `ModuleRegistry.loadModule` no longer returns the raw `ModuleManifest`; it now returns only the loaded module's id, so every consumer must go through the narrow, activation-filtered projection getters (`getDatabases`, `getAgentTools`, `getTasks`, etc.).\n- **Medium correctness finding**: `claimCrossModuleIdentifiers` was non-atomic — a module colliding partway through its own claims (e.g. its second database key) left its earlier keys registered to a module that was never actually added to the registry, corrupting future loads. It's now check-then-commit: every candidate identifier is validated against existing owners and against duplicates within the same manifest before anything is claimed.\n- **Low-priority coverage gaps**: added tests for `getCapabilities()`'s cross-module dedup/activation filtering, and duplicate-name rejection for agent tool, task, and worker names, plus a regression test proving the atomic-claim fix.\n\nThe local branch had also fallen behind the remote (which had picked up automatic `develop` merges via PR #292/#293's branch-update commits), so I rebased my fix commit onto the current remote tip before pushing — no conflicts.\n\nVerified on the final state: `tsc --noEmit` clean, `pnpm -r run build` clean across all packages, and the full `vitest run` suite passes (27 test files, 341 tests).\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
